{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:8fab195f6150fc47","name":"Tuk'ata","source":{"id":"source:reference-8fab195f6150fc47","title":"Tuk'ata","revision":20559,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:05:14Z","sha256":"76d65a5a1c90f923ce803ce7536d20f2bc80630a8c67857759c2b33893e13a5a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20559","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Tuk%27ata&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-8fab195f6150fc47","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Tuk'ata Sith Hounds were native to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"},", the infamous necropolis world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},". The hounds made excellent subjects for the ancient Sith Lords' experiments. They gained additional horns, their size doubled, and their masters imbued them with greater brain mass, increasing their animal cunning. The new creatures guarded the tombs of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"}," with deadly efficiency.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The beasts are later seen in other Sith strongholds as well. They become a favorite of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exar Kun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exar_Kun","referenceId":"reference:ecc01bec6de14936"},", who often assigns the creatures to protect Sith holdings across the galaxy. The hounds are strangely loyal to those attuned to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," know the fragile state of trust all too well, making the Tuk'ata the perfect guardians.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The gleam of malevolence in the yellow eyes of a Tuk'ata Sith Hound is enough to give any Jedi pause. Beast packs often use tactics much too sophisticated for beasts. The worst mistake a Jedi can make is to underestimate them and treat them as common beasts.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tuk'ata Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["One or two Tuk'ata are enough to discourage low-level characters from snooping around Sith sites. The Sith alchemical process has forever transformed these beasts into evil guardians assigned to watch over the darkest places in the galaxy. A pack of Tuk'ata is a worthy threat for higher-level heroes. They could be encountered in the wild, or they could be sent by an unrevealed Sith adversary wishing to observe how the heroes handle themselves in a fight against the beasts.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Tuk'ata Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 14\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," Scent, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +